  "_fixed": true,
  "content_en": "Chapter 1: In just a few days of running together in the royal palace, friendship grew quietly in the dark, and trust also grew up. It's just that none of them noticed that there was another kind of emotion that was slowly growing up silently. The clouds in the sky became more and more serious. Looking at the dome that was gradually covered by dark gray, Aran quickened his pace. \"It's going to rain. There is a ruined temple ahead. We can go and take shelter.\" \"Okay.\" Luo Xue agreed quickly. As soon as I walked into the ruined temple, heavy raindrops fell from the sky, turning into a water barrier in an instant. \"I almost got wet.\" A Ran said, standing at the door and looking at the heavy rain outside. Luo Xue came over. \"Yeah, if it's a little later, it might be a drowned rat. If it rains on Ah Chang...\" \"We are lucky now. Why is your sister so weak?\" \"I heard from my aunt that my mother was not in good health when she was born. Plus, my sister was not born full term. \"Oh, that's it.\" A Ran changed the topic, \"You go in, I'll look for hay or something in the temple.\" Luo Xue returned to Luo Shang and held Luo Shang in her arms. \"Is it cold?\" Luo Shang shook her head, \"Not cold.\" Luo Shang always spoke very few words, so little that sometimes she wouldn't say a word for a whole day. No one knew what was in her closed inner world. This made Luo Xue very distressed, but there was nothing she could do about it. It was raining heavily outside, and the dilapidated house was filled with a chilly coldness. Luo Xue couldn't help but hug Luo Shang tightly. I don’t know how long it took, but A Ran came over carrying some branches and firewood. After a short while, an orange spark bloomed in front of them, bringing them a long-lost warmth. A Ran sat aside and used the wooden stick in his hand to poke at the fire. \"We can't find food. We are going to be hungry.\" Luo Xue lowered her head and looked at Luo Shang, \"A Shang, are you hungry?\" Luo Shang smiled and shook his head. After sweeping around, Luo Xue asked, \"What kind of temple was this originally?\" \"Yuelao Temple has been abandoned for many years. Master brought me here before.\" Aran responded. \"What about your master?\" \"Dead.\" When he said that, a trace of sadness flashed across Aran's face. This made Luo Xue think of Jiuquan's parents who had buried her. She knew the pain of losing a loved one. \"Don't be sad.\" Aran smiled calmly, \"I have stopped being sad a long time ago. My only regret is that I am not good at studying and only learned \"Butterfly Sorrow\".\" \"Is it your master's favorite song?\" \"Well, he said that this song was passed down from the palace. It tells the life of a concubine. She entered the palace at the age of sixteen and experienced being beaten and punished. There was a girl with her. They relied on each other and thought that this was the way they were. In the death palace, a lucky chance changed her fate. She was favored, but it also planted the seeds of tragedy. She kept the girl by her side. Although the relationship was between master and servant, the sisterhood was self-evident. Later, for some reason, Long Yan was furious and demoted her to the cold palace. Living in the cold palace, she vaguely learned from her nun that there was a witch doll hidden under her bed, and she understood that the birthday of the emperor was written on it. It must have been a girl, but she couldn't figure out why someone who loved her would kill her. Behind the cold palace was a garden full of butterflies, which was once called Butterfly Valley, but it was abandoned and no one went there. Later, no one found a female corpse lying in the grass where the butterflies flew. The female corpse experienced butterfly luck every day, but the emperor didn't know about it. I started wandering, and my master told me that if you go in the direction of the sun, you will see hope. However, the master who was suffering from illness said that he wanted to return to his hometown, so he took me to Yunnan. In fact, I really wanted to go to the capital to find out if there is a Butterfly Valley. \"Look in the direction of the sun and you will see hope.\" This is the meaning of the Buluo tribe. Aran's master is probably also a member of the Buluo tribe? People of the Buluo tribe believe in the sun and firmly believe that only fallen leaves can return to their roots to be protected by the sun. \"Has your master been buried?\" \"Yes, I can't find the master's hometown.\" \"There is a mountain halfway up the Zhuri Peak we walked through. Walking half way into the small village, you will see a peach forest. In the middle of the forest are unexpected tombs. I think that is the destination your master is looking for.\" \"How do you know?\" A Ran stroked the flute with his hand. Luo Xue didn't answer. \"There is a small thatched hut next to the peach forest. The house is public. Every year, people who miss their loved ones go there.Stay here for a few days. \"It's already been buried. Let's just let the master rest in peace.\" \"Aran stood up and said, \"When the rain stops, we can reach Dali in half a day's walk. \"Well, will we get separated?\" Luo Xue couldn't help but become worried. Aran looked at her, thought for a moment, and took out a crescent-shaped jade from his arms, \"This was given to me by my master. Take it, and if you get separated, chop up some leaves, take the juice, and apply it on it. Find an obvious place to mark it, and I will follow the mark to find you.\" \"Taking the jade pendant, Luo Xue took off the sun blood stone from her neck, which symbolized the Buluo tribe, and put it in A Ran's hand, \"I'll give this to you too. \"\"good. \"After a night of rain, the green mountains and forests looked particularly clean. Dali was a strange city in Luo Xue's eyes, but A Ran said that Dali was beautiful, so it became the place Luo Xue longed for in her heart. She imagined that Dali was a paradise like the non-Luo people. After a half-day trip, Dali finally arrived. It was not as beautiful as imagined, and the city, which had been filled with war, felt desolate. The streets were full of traces of being swept away, and the barbarians had already come. Seeing this, Luo Xue held Luo Shang's hand tightly, and she told herself that as long as Luo Shang was still there, as long as Aran was still there, there was no need to worry. \"Aran sighed. \"I think there are still some people who have not left. Let's go get some food. \" Luo Xue nodded and followed A Ran. The devastated and decadent scene came into her sight. Why is there a war? Why do the barbarian armies not even let go of the Buluo people who live deep in the mountains? God knows, when I grow up, I will definitely ask you to get it back! \"I said you should hold Ah Chang and follow closely. What if I lose it? \"A Ran complained about Luo Xue, who had been left far behind. \"Huh? oh! \"With that said, he took Luo Shang and ran a few steps, catching up with A Ran in the middle of the street. \"Get out of the way! Get out of the way! \"A fierce sound came from the distance, which was particularly harsh against the sound of horse hooves. The sparse crowd on the street was frightened by the sound and fled to both sides. Luo Xue was involuntarily pushed to the street by others. A group of cavalry came in and galloped past in a mighty manner, kicking up a cloud of dust. \"Cough, cough. \"After coughing twice, I realized that Luo Shang was gone, and so was A Ran. \"A Shang, A Ran, where are you? \"She shouted hard, but no one agreed. Loneliness and helplessness surrounded Luo Xue. She picked up the vegetable leaves on the ground, chopped them with stones, took out the jade pendant, dipped it in the juice, and stamped it on the wall. She repeated this all the way. A few days later, there was still no him. A few days ago, there were rotten vegetables and leaves on the street. Now, a few days later, there is nothing. What should I use as a mark? Ah Ran, is Ah Chang with you? \"How should I contact you? \"Ah Chang, Ah Ran, where are you? Luo Xue shouted over and over in despair. When she got tired of shouting, she leaned against the wall for a while, \"How can I find you?\" \"\"What’s wrong with you? \"Yang Hu looked at Luo Xue friendlyly. \"Are you lost with your family? \"\"Um. Luo Xue nodded. \"I'll take you to find it, are you willing?\" \" Luo Xue, who had no strength at all, neither nodded nor shook her head. Yang Hu picked up Luo Xue, who was leaning against the wall, and walked on the empty and messy street. He took out a piece of cake from his arms and handed it to Luo Xue, \"You eat it, I will hold you. If you see your relatives, call out. \"With Yang Hu's company, Luo Xue searched for three days in Dali City, but the result was still the same. \"I'm afraid your relatives have left, why don't you come with me? Yang Hu looked at Luo Xue and said, \"I don't have children. From now on we will be father and daughter. Are you willing?\" \"...Yang Hu took Luo Xue to Meiyuan in the capital and told her that from now on she would be the miss of Meiyuan. If the miss looks like a miss, she must be proficient in music, chess, calligraphy and painting. After that, Luo Xue became Miss Meiyuan, growing up slowly according to Yang Hu's wishes, becoming smart, smart and pleasing to everyone. Love it. Occasionally, Yang Hu would take Luo Xue shopping. Whatever Luo Xue liked, Yang Hu would give her. Once, Luo Xue met Xiao Xi who had grass in her head and was being sold at a low price. She couldn't help but think of the lost Luo Shang, and she suddenly felt pity for her and begged Yang Hu to buy her. \"In the plum garden, Luo Xue was washing Xiao happy. \"I am eleven years old this year. \"Eleven years old, the same age as Luo Shang. Luo Shang, where are you now? \"What's your name?\" \"My name is Xiaoxi.\" \"Will you stay with me from now on?\" Read together and listen to your teacher's lectures together? \"Okay, Xiaoxi is willing to accompany the lady.\" \"From then on,There is a naughty girl beside Luo Xue, who grows up with her all the way. ...\"Miss!\" Xiao happy shook the dazed Luo Xue. \"Ah?\" Luo Xue responded dully. \"Miss, I've been trapped in the small house like this for a month. Let's go for a walk!\" \"Where to go?\" \"Miss said that she would take Xiaoxi to the garden. It's been half a month, Miss, I'm afraid she has forgotten?\" Luo Xue stood up, walked to the window, propped up the window with a wooden stick, the sun was shining brightly, and there were birdsong in her ears. \"The weather is really nice. Xiao Xi, let's go. You and Xi Yi have been bored with me for half a month.\" \"Okay, we can finally go out.\" It's really been too long. When we just arrived in the garden, Xiao happy looked left and right, looking particularly active. \"Xi Yi, it's so beautiful here. Spring has come!\" Xi Yi ignored her and stayed by Luo Xue's side attentively. You probably won’t meet the princess, right? Luo Xue was still resistant to the princess. \"Miss, look!\" Xiao happy pulled Luo Xue and pointed forward. Following the direction of Xiao happy's finger, Luo Xue saw two people playing chess sitting in front of the stone table in the garden.",
